WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.059 --> 00:00:15.200
chair was placed at the opposite end of the table from the earl's.

2
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.321
"This is a big chair," Cedric said, patting the arms.

3
00:00:20.341 --> 00:00:26.703
"Everything I've seen in this castle is huge—the furniture, the rooms.

4
00:00:27.744 --> 00:00:28.764
Even your dog!"

5
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.701
"And does that bother you?"

6
00:00:33.341 --> 00:00:36.022
the earl asked, picking up a soup spoon.

7
00:00:36.042 --> 00:00:38.782
"Don't worry about me.

8
00:00:39.883 --> 00:00:41.003
I'll get used to it."

9
00:00:42.223 --> 00:00:44.344
Cedric looked down the long table.

10
00:00:46.685 --> 00:00:50.386
He was dazzled by the gleaming glasses, china, and silverware.

11
00:00:52.486 --> 00:00:55.147
Once again the earl had some positive thoughts about Cedric.

12
00:00:55.167 --> 00:01:00.564
"When the boy committed himself to helping me, he didn't give up.

13
00:01:01.705 --> 00:01:03.966
Even when it was clearly too much for him.

14
00:01:05.146 --> 00:01:08.647
And now he's refusing to admit that he's overwhelmed."

15
00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:13.589
"I hate to mention this," Cedric said.

16
00:01:13.609 --> 00:01:17.090
"But I notice you're not wearing your coronet."

17
00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:23.952
"No, it's only for special occasions like a coronation of a king or queen."

18
00:01:26.068 --> 00:01:30.509
"Mr. Hobbs thought an earl always wore a coronet," Cedric said.

19
00:01:30.529 --> 00:01:35.511
"But I thought you must take it off sometimes to put on your hat."

20
00:01:35.531 --> 00:01:38.432
"That's right."

21
00:01:39.492 --> 00:01:41.813
His grandfather almost smiled.

22
00:01:41.833 --> 00:01:44.473
"I don't often wear it."

23
00:01:46.214 --> 00:01:48.875
The earl turned to the footman standing nearby.

24
00:01:48.895 --> 00:01:52.976
"Please tell the cook that the soup is delicious."

25
00:01:54.348 --> 00:01:56.810
The footman raised his eyebrows in surprise.

26
00:01:57.971 --> 00:02:01.535
If the earl had a message for the cook, it was usually a complaint.

27
00:02:05.398 --> 00:02:07.980
Cedric finished eating and leaned back in his chair.

28
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.923
"You must be proud of this house.

29
00:02:11.944 --> 00:02:15.507
I'm only nine, so I haven't been to a lot of places.

30
00:02:16.508 --> 00:02:20.472
But this is the most beautiful house I've ever seen."

31
00:02:22.088 --> 00:02:24.410
"And you think I should be proud of it?"

32
00:02:25.331 --> 00:02:27.573
The earl took a sip from his water glass.

33
00:02:27.593 --> 00:02:31.316
"I'd be proud if it were my house.

34
00:02:32.257 --> 00:02:36.120
Everything about it is beautiful, including the trees in the park."

35
00:02:37.941 --> 00:02:40.503
Cedric paused and looked at the earl uncertainly.

36
00:02:40.523 --> 00:02:47.689
"It's a very big house for just two people to live in," Cedric went on.

37
00:02:47.709 --> 00:02:56.551
"If two people lived here and they weren't good friends He hesitated and played with his napkin.

38
00:02:56.571 --> 00:03:00.734
"They might feel lonely sometimes."

39
00:03:02.174 --> 00:03:05.076
"Do you think we'll be good friends?"

40
00:03:05.096 --> 00:03:09.138
"I think so," Cedric replied.

41
00:03:09.158 --> 00:03:11.800
"Mr. Hobbs and I were great friends.

42
00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.882
He was the best friend I had except my mother."

43
00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:18.944
Cedric was trying not to think of her, but that was impossible.

44
00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.882
This was the first night they'd ever been apart.

45
00:03:25.604 --> 00:03:28.646
The more he thought about his mother, the quieter he became.

46
00:03:30.088 --> 00:03:33.010
Even the earl noticed that he looked tired and sad.

47
00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:38.475
"Come here, Cedric, and help me back to the library."

48
00:03:40.537 --> 00:03:43.900
This time the earl did not lean so heavily on Cedric's shoulder.

49
00:03:46.342 --> 00:03:48.704
Cedric sat on the hearth rug near Dougal.

50
00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:54.203
For a few minutes, he stroked the dog's ears and looked at the fire.

51
00:03:57.646 --> 00:03:59.507
Once or twice he gave a sigh.

52
00:03:59.527 --> 00:04:03.330
"What are you thinking about?"

53
00:04:03.851 --> 00:04:04.852
the earl asked.

54
00:04:04.872 --> 00:04:15.080
"I was thinking about my mother and and I need to walk around the room."

55
00:04:16.521 --> 00:04:19.724
The earl watched as Cedric worked to control his emotions.

56
00:04:24.396 --> 00:04:27.698
Dougal followed the boy, and Cedric laid a hand on his head.

57
00:04:27.718 --> 00:04:32.262
"He's a very nice dog," Cedric said.

58
00:04:32.282 --> 00:04:34.924
"I think he knows how I feel."

59
00:04:34.944 --> 00:04:38.446
"And how do you feel?"

60
00:04:39.647 --> 00:04:42.869
The earl didn't like watching his grandson struggle with homesickness.

61
00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:47.132
But he was proud that Cedric was making an effort to cope.

62
00:04:48.533 --> 00:04:52.116
When Cedric didn't reply, the earl said, "Come here."

63
00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:55.981
Cedric stepped closer.

64
00:04:56.001 --> 00:05:02.085
"Staying all night in another person's castle feels strange," he said.

65
00:05:02.105 --> 00:05:06.468
"Mama told me to remember that she isn't far away.

66
00:05:07.729 --> 00:05:10.070
And I can always look at the picture she gave me."

67
00:05:11.772 --> 00:05:16.715
Cedric leaned against the arm of the earl's chair and against the old man's arm too.

68
00:05:18.696 --> 00:05:21.158
He pulled a velvet-covered case from his pocket.

69
00:05:21.178 --> 00:05:26.174
"You press this button, and it opens, and there she is!"

70
00:05:28.175 --> 00:05:29.977
He looked up at the earl with a smile.

71
00:05:29.997 --> 00:05:33.460
"I don't want to see a picture of that woman!"

72
00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:34.741
the earl thought.

73
00:05:36.062 --> 00:05:37.223
But he looked anyway.

74
00:05:38.704 --> 00:05:41.186
He was surprised at how young and pretty she was.

75
00:05:41.206 --> 00:05:47.211
"I suppose you think you're fond of her," the earl said.

76
00:05:47.231 --> 00:05:51.114
"Oh, yes," Cedric replied.

77
00:05:51.134 --> 00:05:54.840
"We always tell each other everything.

78
00:05:56.141 --> 00:05:59.982
When I'm grown up, I'm going to work and take care of her."

79
00:06:00.002 --> 00:06:04.843
"What kind of job do you think you'll have?"

80
00:06:05.443 --> 00:06:08.664
the earl asked, even though he knew his heir would never work.

81
00:06:08.684 --> 00:06:13.186
"I'm not really sure," Cedric said.

82
00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:16.547
"Maybe I'll be a grocer like Mr.

83
00:06:16.587 --> 00:06:20.568
Hobbs." The earl's eyes widened in horror.

84
00:06:23.744 --> 00:06:25.047
Half an hour later, Mr.

85
00:06:25.087 --> 00:06:26.690
Havisham entered the library.

86
00:06:27.873 --> 00:06:30.177
Before he could speak, the earl hushed him.

87
00:06:32.141 --> 00:06:34.987
Cedric and Dougal were fast asleep in front of the fire.
